      "created_at": "2018-10-27T15:05:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-27T15:06:29Z",
      "body": "As I was thinking more on these recently, what about something we do more obvious to make the user aware of the newly introduced privacy policy? Something like opening with a window when Moonshine next time start with v1.16.0, describing with the privacy policy and force the user to agree to enter Moonshine. We can keep a flag to cookie to not to shown up the window again when next time Moonshine starts (if once agreed by the user).\r\n\r\nI see a few advantage of this system:\r\n\r\n1. User surely be aware of the newly introduce privacy policy by Moonshine\r\n2. User will bound to be align with the privacy policy proposed (they never able to say we were not agreed at any circumstances)\r\n3. We can use the same window system 'if' at sometime we require to update/change the privacy policy \r\n\r\nIn my opinion, user will not be able to use the system if not accept by the terms, so that we can be assure by the new privacy policy laws enforced by the Apple/EU.\r\n",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
