      "created_at": "2019-02-08T04:17:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-02-08T04:35:48Z",
      "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> @JoelProminic , @JustinProminic - I have added privacy policy to Moonshine - it's under menu **Help** -> **Privacy Policy**. However I have one issue. I loaded privacy policy from HTML, because it's the easiest way of displaying it and have looking as it is in document.\r\n> In order to load that html I used class called [FlexHTMLLoader](https://flex.apache.org/asdoc/mx/core/FlexHTMLLoader.html). In order to display what's is loaded I need to use UIComponent class, FlexHTMLLoader cannot be added to spark components. Unfortunately UIComponent doesn't have scrollbar, so I need to work a bit more in order to add those to displayed html. Currently you can scroll all content by mouse, but scrollbar is not visible.\r\n> We can move slowly forward with release - I will try to work on that tomorrow more.\r\n\r\nPlease ensure the API do not use HTML API in-background. We can not bundle WebKit to the App Store version, they'll reject it.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand as an alternative, we can display the texts in-Moonshine as plain texts to an editor/tab and make it uneditable. \r\n\r\n[Edit: I noticed the link does navigates to browser later, instead of using Webkit]",
